1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,404
Turns out, a few everyday foods could be the reason your hands and feet feel numb, cold, or swollen by the end of the day.

2
00:00:08,724 --> 00:00:14,428
When blood vessels narrow and circulation slows down, that's usually what's driving it.

3
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:22,449
Too much sodium makes your body hold onto extra fluid, and too much saturated fat builds up along the vessel walls.

4
00:00:22,769 --> 00:00:29,112
Deli meat, fried food, and sugary soda are three of the biggest everyday culprits.

5
00:00:29,432 --> 00:00:43,061
A two-ounce serving of deli turkey packs around 570 milligrams of sodium - that's more than a third of the American Heart Association's ideal daily limit, in just one sandwich.

6
00:00:43,381 --> 00:00:49,868
Freshly roasted chicken breast at the deli counter is a much lower-sodium swap than cured meats.

7
00:00:50,188 --> 00:00:56,563
If you do stick with packaged deli meat, check the label for a low-sodium or no-salt-added version.

8
00:00:56,883 --> 00:00:58,321
Fried food is next.

9
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:08,515
Regularly eating it is linked to higher rates of heart disease and stroke - the trans fat in the oil raises LDL cholesterol and damages artery walls over time.

10
00:01:08,835 --> 00:01:16,201
Air-frying or baking at home uses a fraction of the oil, and grilled or roasted options are an easy swap when you're eating out.

11
00:01:16,521 --> 00:01:18,230
Sugary soda is the third one.

12
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:24,493
Just one sugary drink a day is linked to a nearly 20 percent higher risk of heart disease.

13
00:01:24,813 --> 00:01:30,437
Swap it for sparkling water with a splash of real fruit juice, or unsweetened iced tea instead.

14
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:36,254
Small swaps in what you reach for add up to real relief for your circulation over time.
